\section{Goals for Next Week}{
% Goals: what you want to accomplish next week.
\p{I am but a humble nomad in my long journey toward TPU sensei-ship. Unfortunately (or fortunately?), I am still firmly on the left end of the [Dunning-Kruger](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dunning–Kruger_effect) curve. I am progressing slowly but very dilligently through the [[scaling-book]]. I want to be on chapter 5 by end of next week. The remaining chapter 3 exercises seem like they may take awhile and chapter 4 is equally important as it is dense, so I want to make sure I give it a proper treatment. An additional mini reading / todo list:}
\ul{
  \li{[[yeCAKECompilerAgentCoDesign2026]] - seems interesting but the paper is kind of bare bones on first pass.}
   \li{Want to be able to read the whole TPU pipeline. This primarily means setting up the TPU infrastructure but also a good set of blogs [here](https://patricktoulme.substack.com/p/when-xla-isnt-enough-from-pallas), [here](https://considerthebulldog.com/tte-tpu/#ref-32), and [here](https://considerthebulldog.com/pallas-sharded-matmuls/).}
\li{Need to come up with definitive proposal for project.}
\ul{
   \li{Limitations / survey of existing approaches.}
\ul{
  \li{Importantly, why non-agentic approaches cannot compete in [JaxBench](tschandJAXBenchBenchmarkingAutonomous2026)-regime.}
   \li{Maybe walk through how each method does GQA?}
}
   \li{Clear benchmarks to test.}
   \li{Be able to defend choice of TPU.}
}
}
\p{As a bit of a [productivity](7BUX) aside, I have noticed that I am wasting a lot of my prime deep work bandwidth in the morning on the transfer / organization of notes into this forest during reading. Additionally, my post-lunch block is very ineffective. I had the genius idea of eliminating the cognitive overhead of organizing and transferring notes by deferring until the afternoon block. In the morning block, I will just dump everything I might care about later. Then, in the later block, I will do the menial, low cognitive demand task of choosing what stays and where it goes. This can also serve as a form of review.}
\p{Furthermore, I have officially setup a technology free desk to take this to the extreme. This will hopefully serve as my paper reading station or when I am rich enough to get physical textbooks. I have an accompanying notebook to write down any questions I need to ask Claude after the pomo block ends, or write down relevant notes to transfer later. I have consistently avoided doing this because I believe quickly asking Claude is a necessity. However, I hope to find that writing down and thinking about questions independently first will not be that bad and may even be useful.}
\p{Until next week!}
